    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0182" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1358</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-29T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1918,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 23, 3 p.m.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d129-f1"/> Get in touch with Masaryk
                    and advise Department fully his views of situation in Russia and possibility of
                    organizing within Russia any effective resistance to Central powers. Also
                    forward any other messages he wishes to transmit. Masaryk well known to
                    Department as Bohemian patriot.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
